	"title": "Self-Administered Comorbidity Questionnaire (SACQ)",
	"description": "The SACQ captures comorbid conditions via patient self-report, evaluating presence, treatment, and impact on daily activities.",
	"purpose": "The Self-Administered Comorbidity Questionnaire (SACQ) is a tool used to assess the presence of comorbidities in patients. It is a self-administered questionnaire designed to help identify various medical conditions or diseases that may coexist with a primary condition, often focusing on common chronic diseases like diabetes, hypertension, or heart disease.",
